course: dictionary
lesson: 1651
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word china can name a country, a set of plates, or a friend in some places. «China also gave the world porcelain, tea, kites and an early earthquake detector.» Things given to the world come from a country, so here China means the country.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. China with a capital C is a proper noun, the name of a place, like London or Paris. Small c, as in «the best china», means fine, hard, white clay made into cups, plates and bowls.
explain: Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence, then swap it in and check. «Carry the china carefully, because it breaks easily» works for plates, not for a country. Slang works the same way: in Britain and Australia, «china» can mean a mate, so you must read the whole sentence to be sure.
fact: China (capital C) is a very large country in East Asia, and its capital is Beijing.
fact: china (small c) is fine, hard, white clay made into cups, plates and bowls.
fact: In UK and Australian slang, «china» means a mate or friend.
fact: «Like a bull in a china shop» means very clumsy, breaking things by accident.
fact: Porcelain is a fine kind of china, and «China also gave the world porcelain» tells us where it began.
exercise: «The best china came out for the guests.» What does china mean here? | A large country in Asia | A tall wall built long ago | A mate or friend | *Fine cups and plates
exercise: «Beijing is the capital of China.» Why is China written with a capital C? | It is the name of a friend | It is a kind of clay | *It is the name of a country | It is the start of a sentence
exercise: Mia says, «Thanks, china!» to her friend in Sydney. What does china mean? | A cup made of clay | A sudden shower of rain | A large country | *A mate or friend
test: «Carry the china carefully, because it breaks easily.» What does china mean here? | A country in East Asia | Carrying a bag | *Cups and plates made of fine clay | Mate or friend
test: «He is like a bull in a china shop.» What does this phrase suggest? | Very tired | Very quiet | Very graceful | *Very clumsy
exam: In «China also gave the world porcelain, tea, kites and an early earthquake detector», which meaning of China fits? | *A large country in East Asia | Fine cups and plates | A bird that sings at night | A friend or mate
